186045417] [17592186550924 #edb/ref 1080 "60%" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550924 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186550924 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ce5f37d0-df7f-5e60-8207-efacf2cdc514" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186550690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551182 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "be770eee-142d-5138-82b0-d774ea34700b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186550924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186550549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551210 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e2414de2-0b71-5f21-ba04-5ccbaa91ec84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551304 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551304 #edb/ref 1069 "q-144037" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551304 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551304 #edb/ref 1071 "A cattle rancher has three ranches, where $34%$ of the rancher's cows are on ranch $A$, $36%$ are on ranch $B,$ and $30%$ on ranch $C.$ If $25%$ of all cows on ranch $A$ and $20%$ of all cows on ranch $B$ are dairy cows, and the probability that a randomly selected cow from any of the three ranches is a dairy cow is $37%,$ what is the probability that a randomly selected cow from ranch $C$ is a dairy cow?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551304 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "87509e91-72b0-5f1f-83b2-ad41631e8459" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551304 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $D$ be the event that a selected cow is a dairy cow, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $A$,\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $B$,\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the cow is from ranch $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability that the randomly selected cow is a dairy cow, we use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation. \n\n- Since $34%$ of all the rancher's cows are on ranch $A$, $36%$ are on ranch $B,$ and $30%$ are on ranch $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.34,\\,P(B)=0.36,\\,P(C)=0.3.\n$$\n\n- Since $25%$ of all cows on ranch $A$ and $20%$ of all cows on ranch $B$ are dairy cows, we have \n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.25,\\,P(D|B)=0.2.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected cow from any of the three ranches is  a dairy cow is $37%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.37.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C) \\\\ 0.37 & =(0.25)(0.34)+(0.2)(0.36)+P(D|C)(0.3) \\\\ 0.37 & =0.085+0.072+0.3P(D|C) \\\\ 0.3P(D|C) & =0.213 \\\\ P(D|C) & =0.71\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected cow from ranch $C$ is a dairy cow is $71%.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551319 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186551182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551319 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143572" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551319 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551319 #edb/ref 1071 "In a hardware store, there are three boxes containing light bulbs. Box $A$ contains $15$ bulbs, of which $2$ are defective. Box $B$ contains $10$ bulbs, of which $1$ is defective. And box $C$ contains $10$ light bulbs, of which $2$ are defective. A box is selected at random, and a bulb is randomly selected from the box. Find the probability that the bulb is defective." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551319 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a3aefa5f-7730-50af-bdda-78228d7a1e41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551319 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $D$ be the event of selecting a defective bulb, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the bulb is from box $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the bulb is from box $B$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the bulb is from box $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a defective bulb at random from one of the three boxes, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D\\cap A)+P(D\\cap B)+P(D\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a box is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $2$ defective bulbs out of $15$  in box $A,$ $1$ defective bulb out of $10$ in box $B,$ and $2$  defective bulbs out of $10$ bulbs in box $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(D|A)=\\frac{2}{15},\\,P(D|B)=\\frac{1}{10},\\,P(D|C)=\\frac{2}{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability of selecting a defective bulb at random from one of the three boxes is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|B)P(B)+P(D|C)P(C) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{15})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{1}{10})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{2}{10})(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{45}+\\frac{1}{30}+\\frac{2}{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{90}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551358 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186551390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551358 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "015fd7cc-296c-527b-8d93-783a3144a040" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551358 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551383 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "330a5393-8793-5481-819f-7f472b79e0cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551383 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186551304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551390 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186551437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551390 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3ab20fd2-6a65-50a2-902a-224e12d123dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186551390 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186436228 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
